-- title:
--   Formal smoothness of the descended Igusa ring over A₀
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero level $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, and a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$). Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ via `hle`, and let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with values in the characteristic-$q$ function field, compatible with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$ (`hR₀`). Let $\pi\in A$ satisfy $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$, let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and let $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ be a family of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ one indexed by $W$, subject to: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ is the Gauss-type ring of quotients $x/y$ of Laurent series over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction; each $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ moving $\infty$ to $\ell$ under $\mathrm{redQ}$; $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ injective and permuted by all such pullbacks; $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ meets $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, is fixed by all those pullbacks, contains a $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for every $a\in A$, and relates to $R_0$ and the place $s$ as in `hSS_over` (elements of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ regular wherever $j$ is and with residue in $s$ land in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, congruent modulo the maximal ideal to the prescribed constant). Further let $K_0$ be a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ containing $\pi$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic, and $A_0$ a henselian discrete valuation domain with an injective local homomorphism $\iota:A_0\to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A\cap K_0$, inducing a surjection onto the residue field of $A$, and with uniformiser $\varpi_0$ satisfying $\iota\varpi_0=\pi$. Let $F_0$ be the subfield of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, assumed to contain $j$, made an $A_0$-algebra through $\iota$. Then for every line $\ell$ and every $A_0$-subalgebra $S$ of $F_0$ whose elements are exactly those of $F_0$ lying in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$, the algebra $A_0\to S$ is formally smooth.
--
--   This identifies the trace on the descended field $F_0$ of the Igusa valuation ring attached to a component $\ell$ of the special fibre as a formally smooth $A_0$-algebra, i.e. the local ring at the generic point of that component of the two-chart integral model is smooth over the henselian base. It feeds the construction of Igusa charts with formally smooth local rings and unique crossings on the normal model generated by $j$.
